// A private channel between this server and the Orion client.
//
// The client already has one: packet 0xFC carries Orion's own messages, with a
// 16-bit command after a 16-bit length. Sphere can hook any packet id from a
// script (PACKET252 in sphere.ini, 252 being 0xFC) and reply on the same
// socket with SENDPACKET - so the two ends can talk about things UO's 1997
// protocol has no opcode for, without touching either codebase.
//
// Locals on entry:
//   ARGN1        the packet id
//   LOCAL.NUM    how many bytes arrived
//   LOCAL.STR    the raw bytes
//   LOCAL.ACCOUNT, LOCAL.CHAR
//   ARGO         the client, for ARGO.SENDPACKET
//
// Returning 1 tells Sphere the packet is handled and should not be processed
// further; 0 lets it fall through to the normal handler.

[FUNCTION f_orion_packet]
SERV.LOG ORION in: packet=<ARGN1> bytes=<LOCAL.NUM> account='<LOCAL.ACCOUNT>'

// Answer with OCT_ORION_FEATURES (50): 0xFC, length 9, command 50, flags.
// The client reads this in PACKET_HANDLER(OrionMessages) and applies it.
ARGO.SENDPACKET B252 W9 W50 D3735928559

SERV.LOG ORION out: OCT_ORION_FEATURES payload=0xDEADBEEF
RETURN 1
